    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW245GLZmEXLJfoqFSif6eB5m)_\n\n## What\n\n- In DEVONthink, select a citation and press `Caps Lock + r`: the record of the cited work opens.\n- Builds on the existing design (`docs/architecture/citation-matching-from-selection.org`) and on `sp-cite-match`; no new matcher.\n- Lookup order:\n  - the reference list at the end of the same document (numeric `[12]` or author-year `(Smith 2017)`);\n  - the BibTeX files, with the `sp-cite-match` scoring and thresholds;\n  - litdb, as a list to choose from (never automatic).\n- A BibTeX match opens through `sp-reading-open`, so the record-lookup code of `sp-devonthink-browse`/`sp-reading` (crossref parent, index-if-missing) is unchanged.\n\n## Files\n\n- `sp-cite-open.el` (+ literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-cite-open.org`) and 9 ERT tests (pass in batch on Emacs 29.3).\n- `hammerspoon/cite-match.lua`: `M.send` takes a protocol; new `M.open`.\n- `hammerspoon/devonthink.lua`: `Caps+r`, DEVONthink only. No clash with Caps+x/c or Caps+Option+1-7 (#512); `r` is not a workspace key.\n- `README.org` module table and design doc updated. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Not done / doubtful\n\n- Citations in running prose are only parsed as surnames plus a year. `Ibid.` and `op. cit.` match nothing.\n- No page jump inside the cited work; the record opens at its start.\n- A PDF without a text layer has no reference list; the selection itself is matched.\n- Not run on the Mac: the DEVONthink AppleScript (`plain text of record`), the hotkey with Caps held, org-protocol.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Stow, reload Hammerspoon, restart the Emacs server; `M-x emacs-version` and `(require 'sp-cite-open)` load without error.\n- [ ] Open a PDF with a numbered reference list in DEVONthink, select `[3]`, press Caps+r: the record of entry 3 opens (or the BibTeX/litdb prompt appears).\n- [ ] Select `(Smith 2017)` for an author-year paper whose list has that entry: the record opens.\n- [ ] Select a whole reference entry that is in your BibTeX: its record opens without a prompt.\n- [ ] Select a citation that is in no BibTeX file: a litdb list appears; choosing a hit opens it.\n- [ ] Select `Mueller 2015` when the list has 2015a and 2015b: you are asked to choose.\n- [ ] Caps+r with nothing selected shows \"nothing was selected\" and does nothing else.\n- [ ] Caps+r in another app does nothing; Ctrl+Shift+K still writes the Cited works section.\n- [ ] Clipboard content is the same after the key as before.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-cite-open-text` with a typed citation works in Emacs without Hammerspoon.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8q5mntJU5gbou4xiT)_",
